86:T109e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the blog hosting really free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Hosting, HTTPS, a free outrankblog.com address and your own domain or subfolder are free up to 10,000 visits a month per blog, with unlimited posts and no ads. No credit card needed. If you use your own domain, you only pay your registrar for it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the catch with free blog hosting?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On most free blog hosts it is the address, ads or a cap. Medium and Substack keep you on their address unless you pay, WordPress.com and Wix show their own ads on free sites, and some free plans cap storage or posts. On Outrank Blogs the one limit is 10,000 visits a month, and you can see the catch on every other platform in our comparison of the best free blogging platforms."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will Google index my blog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, from day one, including on your free outrankblog.com address. Connect your own domain or subfolder, also free, so every post builds your own site's authority. Blogs that break our content policy stay hidden from search engines until they move to their own domain."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will ChatGPT and other AI assistants read my blog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every blog has an llms.txt file, a Markdown copy of every post, structured data and pages rendered on the server, and its robots.txt lets AI crawlers in. It matters: in our study of 96 questions, 74% of the sources ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Claude cited were blog content, and 99% of those blog posts were on the company's own site."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use my own domain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Connect a subdomain like blog.yourbrand.com, a subfolder like yourbrand.com/blog, or a domain used only for the blog. We give y